# Change approval for high-risk paths (D959, D988; SOC 2 CC8.1).
#
# This package is published to npm and runs on customers' machines, so a change to how
# it is built, versioned or published needs an approving review from @cbrock84 before it
# merges. Everything else merges on green checks (D850). The file only takes effect while
# the repository's "main protection" ruleset has "Require review from Code Owners" on.
#
# There is deliberately no catch-all `*` rule: that would put a human review on every
# pull request, which D959 did not choose.

# This file itself, so a pull request cannot drop a path without the approval it needs.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @cbrock84

# Workflows. publish.yml publishes to npm with OIDC trusted publishing.
/.github/workflows/ @cbrock84

# The manifest and lockfile decide what ships, its version, and what runs on install.
/package.json @cbrock84
/package-lock.json @cbrock84
